# Brief — Third Eye World

> The north star. Read this before touching anything. If a decision conflicts with this file, this file wins (after the ten non-negotiables in §3).

## What we are building

A **voice-first, blind-first social network** for blind and low-vision (BLV) people. Nonprofit, free, open-source, no ads.

Built *from sound first* — not a visual product with accessibility bolted on. **The rule that governs every ticket:** if it starts from "the screen shows…" and works backward to audio, it is rejected.

## The problem (why this exists)

**Loneliness — not engagement.** Vision impairment correlates strongly with social isolation (≈half of visually impaired adults report at least moderate loneliness). Success is measured against a validated loneliness instrument (UCLA Loneliness Scale), **never** time-on-app, streaks, or vanity counts.

## The core loop (the entire product)

1. Record a short **voice memo** — 90s soft cap, 3min hard cap.
2. The timeline **plays memos back-to-back, like radio.**
3. You can **like, comment (by voice), or skip.** That is the whole interaction set.

**Deliberately absent:** follow graph · ranking/recommendation algorithm · follower/like/view counts · images/video · infinite scroll (the stream *ends*).

## Delivery order (settled)

**Web first → native iOS → native Android.** Private messaging (E2EE) ships with the phone apps, not the website.

```
Slice 0  Walking skeleton (web): record → radio timeline → 3-route controls, screen-reader-correct
Slice 1  Transcripts (auto, correctable) + channels/stations + transcript search
Slice 2  Auth (passkeys / magic link / phone OTP — equal status) + accessible moderator console
Slice 3  Backend hardening: object storage, self-hosted Whisper (LID→ASR), Piper TTS
Slice 4  Native iOS (SwiftUI) — full UIAccessibility, media-transport controls, audio ducking
Slice 5  Native Android (Compose) — TalkBack, Media3 MediaSessionService
Slice 6  E2EE DMs (libsignal) on phone apps — request queue, franking, scam interstitials
Slice 7  IVR dial-in path (basic-phone reach) + data-saver mode
```

Each slice is a **vertical slice** that proves the ontology end-to-end, not a horizontal layer. Nothing is scaffolded ahead of the slice that needs it.

## Success gates (go/no-go)

- ≥90% task completion by real screen-reader users on core flows, across NVDA/JAWS/VoiceOver/TalkBack.
- Zero unresolved critical accessibility defects.
- Transcript label + correction loop working.
- ≥99.5% crash-free sessions.
- Loneliness instrument administrable accessibly, with consent.

## The two hardest calls (recorded, not smoothed over)

- **No sign-language video.** It would force video, breaking three commitments (no video, low-bandwidth reach, audio-only identity). Instead: **text memos are first-class**, read aloud into the stream by synthetic voice, readable on refreshable braille displays (serves the DeafBlind community). No signing avatars. Dissent recorded: for many culturally Deaf people text is a second language — the product does not claim text equals signing.
- **Control scheme reversal.** Volume-button and whole-screen-tap controls are out (Apple policy / OS-inconsistent / screen-reader-intercepted). In: **media-transport controls + voice commands + screen-reader custom actions + plain on-screen buttons** — every action reachable three ways.

